title: Transcripts are deleted after thirty days, so the account keeps rows whose transcripts are gone.
pid: 45f53beb-7ca1-42a9-94d8-104b3e25d01a
body: |2-
  Claude Code removes transcripts older than its 'cleanupPeriodDays'
  setting, 30 by default, which 'my-dot-claude/settings.json' does not
  change. Rebuilding the account from nothing would lose them; running
  the script again replaces only rows whose transcripts still exist,
  and keeps those rows' requests the same way. Since the pacer runs it
  after each session, a row is lost only if neither the pacer nor anyone
  runs it for a month. The weighted price is recomputed from the
  requests on every run, so a changed weight reaches the rows of
  deleted transcripts too. I have not yet seen a deletion happen here.
